<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Human sacrifice</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as sacrificial</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Human sacrifice is the ritual killing of people as an offering to gods or spirits. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> it was central to religion, intended to sustain the gods and the cosmic order. The need for captives shaped Aztec warfare, including the ritualised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flower-wars">Flower Wars</a>, and was tied to tribute and imperial power.</p></div>
